            <ArticleTitle>Suspended Manufacture of Biological Structures.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/adma.201605594</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A method for the production of complex cell-laden structures is reported, which allows high-levels of spatial control over mechanical and chemical properties. The potential of this method for producing complicated tissues is demonstrated by manufacturing a complex hard/soft tissue interface and demonstrating that cell phenotype can be maintained over four weeks of culture.</AbstractText>
